# Deals — /api/deals
#
# Run `dotnet run --project JsonApiPoc` first, then click the gutter icon next to a request.
# `###` separates requests; the text after it is the request name. "->" notes the expected outcome.
#
# Seed: 1 Acme - ERP integration (proposal, contact Jan, owner Sarah)
#       2 Globex - fleet tracking pilot (qualified)
#       3 Initech - support renewal (won)
#       4 Acme - hardware upgrade (lead, NO contact — the empty to-one)
#       5 Globex - warehouse expansion (lost)
# Stages: lead | qualified | proposal | won | lost.
# Custom fields on deals: probability (number), competitor (text), contractSignedDate (date).
#
# The write endpoints take flat JSON, not JSON:API resource documents — this API is read-side
# JSON:API only. Requests below mutate the local SQLite database.

@host = http://localhost:5031

### List deals
GET {{host}}/api/deals
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### With company, contact, and owner side-loaded (multi-include compound document)
GET {{host}}/api/deals?include=company,contact,owner
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Filtered by pipeline stage
GET {{host}}/api/deals?filter[stage]=proposal&include=company
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Sorted by amount, biggest first (sort composes with paging links)
GET {{host}}/api/deals?sort=-amount
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Sorted by close date, then title
GET {{host}}/api/deals?sort=closeDate,title
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Mixed directions: grouped by stage ascending, biggest amount first within each stage
GET {{host}}/api/deals?sort=stage,-amount
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Second page of 2 -> links.prev/next, meta.total
GET {{host}}/api/deals?page[number]=2&page[size]=2
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Kitchen sink: filter + include + sort + sparse fieldsets + paging in one request
GET {{host}}/api/deals?filter[stage]=proposal&include=company,owner&sort=-amount&fields[deals]=title,amount,company,owner&fields[companies]=name&fields[users]=name&page[number]=1&page[size]=5
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Single deal (note customFields in attributes and links.self on every resource)
GET {{host}}/api/deals/1?include=contact,owner
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Sparse fieldset on a single resource
GET {{host}}/api/deals/1?fields[deals]=title,stage
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Missing deal -> 404
GET {{host}}/api/deals/999
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Following the hypermedia links. Each relationship carries links.self (the
# linkage) and links.related (the full related resource).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Related resource: a deal's company (links.related)
GET {{host}}/api/deals/1/company
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Relationship linkage: just the resource identifier (links.self)
GET {{host}}/api/deals/1/relationships/company
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### A deal's contact
GET {{host}}/api/deals/1/contact
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### A deal's contact linkage
GET {{host}}/api/deals/1/relationships/contact
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### A deal's owner, trimmed with a sparse fieldset
GET {{host}}/api/deals/1/owner?fields[users]=name
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### A deal's owner linkage
GET {{host}}/api/deals/1/relationships/owner
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Empty to-one related resource -> 200 with data: null (deal 4 has no contact; not a 404)
GET {{host}}/api/deals/4/contact
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Empty to-one linkage -> 200 with data: null
GET {{host}}/api/deals/4/relationships/contact
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Relationship on a missing parent -> 404
GET {{host}}/api/deals/999/relationships/company
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Query validation -> 400 problem details
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Unsupported include path -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/deals?include=invoices
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Unknown stage filter -> 400 (allowed values listed in detail)
GET {{host}}/api/deals?filter[stage]=bogus
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Undeclared filter name -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/deals?filter[amount]=48000
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Unsupported sort field -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/deals?sort=height
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Unknown query parameter -> 400 (strict validation)
GET {{host}}/api/deals?foo=bar
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Paging a single-resource endpoint -> 400 (only collections paginate)
GET {{host}}/api/deals/1?page[number]=2
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Unknown field in a sparse fieldset -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/deals?fields[deals]=nonexistent
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Writes: flat JSON bodies (deliberately not JSON:API documents)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Create a deal with custom fields -> 201 + Location + the created resource document
POST {{host}}/api/deals
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Globex - warehouse automation",
  "amount": 95000,
  "stage": "qualified",
  "closeDate": "2026-11-30T00:00:00Z",
  "companyId": 2,
  "contactId": 3,
  "ownerId": 2,
  "customFields": {
    "probability": 40,
    "competitor": "Siemens"
  }
}

### Unknown stage -> 422
POST {{host}}/api/deals
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Bad stage", "stage": "bogus", "companyId": 1, "ownerId": 1 }

### Unknown custom field -> 422
POST {{host}}/api/deals
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Bad deal",
  "companyId": 1,
  "ownerId": 1,
  "customFields": { "nonexistent": 1 }
}

### Referencing a missing company -> 422
POST {{host}}/api/deals
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Orphan deal", "companyId": 999, "ownerId": 1 }

### Update partially -> 204, no body; omitted fields keep their value, customFields merge
PATCH {{host}}/api/deals/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stage": "won",
  "amount": 120000,
  "customFields": { "probability": 100 }
}

### Re-point a deal's contact via flat PATCH (this API's substitute for relationship writes)
PATCH {{host}}/api/deals/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "contactId": 2 }

### Update with an unknown stage -> 422
PATCH {{host}}/api/deals/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "stage": "bogus" }

### Update a missing deal -> 404
PATCH {{host}}/api/deals/999
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Ghost" }

### Delete a deal (its custom field values go with it) -> 204
DELETE {{host}}/api/deals/5

### Delete a missing deal -> 404
DELETE {{host}}/api/deals/999
